File name: e1-what.png. Landscape, exactly 1536 x 1024. References: refs/desktop-groups.jpg (copy its layout closely).
Screen: the Off Grid AI browser extension's welcome page, opened in a browser tab right after install. Step 1 of 5.
Top left mono label "OFF GRID AI · IN YOUR BROWSER". Title "What do you want to do?". Muted line under it "Pick any. Next you choose the details."
A grid of five tiles (three in the first row, two in the second), each with a line icon at top left, a name and a muted one-line description at the bottom:
1 "Chat and ask" — "Questions about any page or photo" (picked)
2 "Create" — "Pictures from a sentence"
3 "Write" — "Fix, rewrite and dictate in any text box" (picked)
4 "Get work done" — "It does the clicking, with your approval"
5 "Private and connected" — "Passwords and sync"
Footer: left muted line "Works with Off Grid AI on your computer. Nothing goes to a cloud." Centre: 5-segment progress, segment 1 active, mono step name "WHAT YOU WANT". Right: text button "Skip, set it up" and the emerald primary button "Continue".
